<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zhang Fu (Ming general)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1375–<a href="/years/1449">1449</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Zhang Fu, Duke of Ying</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zhang Fu was a Ming general who served in the 1406 to 1407 invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> that overthrew the Ho dynasty and created <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiaozhi">Jiaozhi</a> province. He returned several times to crush resistance, capturing the Later Tran rulers Gian Dinh in 1409 and Trung Quang in 1414. He was killed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tumu-crisis">Tumu Crisis</a> in 1449.</p></div>
